# ENGINE_1 -- Ideas

Use when the user has a raw idea and has not yet scaffolded. Do not implement
the bundle here. If the idea cannot name what a frontier model gets wrong on
the first attempt, **stop**. If the remaining work is a ticket rather than a
collection-scale system, **stop**. Horizon is decided here; traps are decided
here. Do not discover either after the zip.

Policy: `docs/odyssey-long-horizon.md` · `docs/odyssey-difficulty-design.md` ·
`docs/odyssey-family-specific-guidance.md`

## Batch checks (all must pass)

| Check | The idea must say |
|---|---|
| Well-specified | What exists in `/app`, what to build, constraints, outputs |
| Verifiable | Absolute paths, schemas, deterministic checks |
| Interesting | Real engineering, not a prototype toy |
| **Long-horizon** | Complete system in the declared family; honest expert remaining work **>= 40 hours**; 4-10h agent budget. Not a feature, repair, slice, or stubbed module |
| **Difficult** | First-attempt trap, decoy or almost-correct algorithm, hidden channel that catches it |
| Solvable | Offline, in-image, oracle can derive |
| Outcome-verified | Artifacts the grader can measure |
| Not recall | Not a textbook/interview exercise a model has seen thousands of times |

## Required reply before scaffolding

```text
Engine: 1
Family: <collectionFamily> / <taskFamily> / <verifierFamily>
Slug candidate: <kebab>
Remaining work (system, not ticket): <one paragraph naming subsystems>
Honest expert hours: <number >= 40>
Agent budget: <4-10h, not 7200s-on-a-ticket>
First-attempt trap: <one paragraph>
Almost-correct algorithm: <what the model will try>
Hidden channel that catches it: <generated / invariant / other>
Decoy plan: <none, because tight library> OR <file off the hot path>
Probe risk if we shipped today: HIGH -- recall | MEDIUM -- one-file fix | LOW -- interacting
Horizon risk if we shipped today: HIGH -- ticket | LOW -- collection-scale system
Ready for ENGINE_3: yes/no
```

`Ready for ENGINE_3: no` if Long-horizon, Difficult, or Not-recall fails. Do
not run `new_task.py` until yes.

## Forbidden

- "It is hard because it takes N hours" as the *trap* (hours are the horizon
  bar; they do not replace a first-attempt trap)
- "It is long-horizon because frontier models fail" (model trials do not
  lengthen a ticket; the judge sees `/app`)
- "Add more requirements" on a well-known algorithm
- Padding `expertTimeEstimateHours` or `timeout_sec` on the same module
  (a 32h merge library still failed this funnel as too short)
- Starting ENGINE_3 to discover difficulty or horizon later
- Ticket shapes: add/fix a feature in an existing parser; one product
  workflow; repair an eval pipeline; implement a small greenfield module
